# clang-tidy C++ profile for the SystemVerilog slang adapter (adapters/slang/*.cpp, *.hpp).
#
# The core is C17, so the repo-root .clang-tidy (docs/DESIGN.md 15.2) disables every
# C++-only check there. clang-tidy finds this file for sources below adapters/slang/ and
# InheritParentConfig appends its Checks block to the root one: the root's family enables,
# WarningsAsErrors and CheckOptions (function size, identifier length, loop-counter names)
# still apply, and this file only adds or narrows.
# third_party/slang is vendored and stays outside the gate: tools/lint.sh's file lists exclude
# third_party/, and its anchored header filter does not match slang's headers.
#
# The parent Checks string ends with the C++-only disables (-bugprone-use-after-move, ...,
# -readability-use-anyofallof). The family re-enables below put those checks back for this
# directory, which is the point of the profile: the adapter runs the C checks where they apply
# to C++ *and* the C++-only ones. Every later -check removes only what is noise for this single
# adapter translation unit, and every removal has its reason here. A re-enabled check that
# produces no finding today stays on for free.
#
# Suppressed -- recursion is the input's shape, not an IR traversal:
#   -misc-no-recursion
#     The adapter is a slang-AST visitor: stmt()/stmtList()/stmtWhile()/stmtRepeat()/
#     stmtTimed() call back into each other over child statements, and the expression visitor
#     (expr/exprLeaf/exprOper and the expr* helpers) recurses over subexpressions; clang-tidy
#     also reports the std::transform lambda call chains that carry them. locOf/ensureBuffer
#     recurse once per included file while mapping a location to its buffer. Module instances
#     are queued with an explicit worklist (queueBody/plans), so the only recursion is over one
#     construct's statement/expression nesting and the include chain. That depth is the parsed
#     source's nesting depth, bounded by the input text itself: slang's own recursive-descent
#     parser and preprocessor walk the same nesting first, so any input deep enough to overflow
#     this walk has already overflowed the parser's stack. It is not the IR traversal DESIGN
#     15.1 forbids (a 2M-node IR list is walked with explicit worklists in src/; adapters are
#     outside the core, D8').
#
# Suppressed -- findings are in the public C ABI header, not in adapter code:
#   -performance-enum-size
#     Fires only on include/odin3/odin3.h (odin3_status, odin3_log_level, ...). Those enums'
#     underlying type is part of the C ABI and of struct layouts; narrowing it is an ABI change,
#     not a lint fix. The check is C++-only, so the C profile never sees it; here every finding
#     is in a C header and is a documented false positive.
#
# Suppressed -- printf-style diagnostics, CERT va_list core in place:
#   -cert-dcl50-cpp
#     failf() is the adapter's one C-style variadic function; it forwards to vsnprintf, which is
#     the CERT-recommended va_list pattern for the work, and its output goes to the C log API.
#     Removing the variadic layer means std::format at every call site, an adapter-wide rewrite
#     with no safety gain.
#
# Suppressed -- include hygiene stays advisory (same policy as the root file):
#   -misc-include-cleaner
#     Re-disabled because misc-* above re-enables it. DESIGN 15.1/15.2 keep
#     include-what-you-use advisory, not blocking.
#
# Suppressed -- modernize style rewrites the adapter does not adopt:
#   -modernize-avoid-c-arrays
#     The five C arrays are deliberate: fixed-size snprintf buffers passed to C string
#     functions, and static const opcode tables iterated as arrays. std::array adds no safety
#     at those sites.
#   -modernize-use-auto
#     The adapter spells out types, widths included (uint32_t ids, SVInt values); auto at the
#     flagged casts hides exactly the type the code cares about. Style only.
#   -modernize-use-trailing-return-type
#     Classical return types are the house and LLVM style used by every definition in the file;
#     the rewrite touches 300+ lines with no semantic change.
#   -modernize-use-using
#     typedef -> using is a pure style rewrite of the file's C-style typedefs (enums, opcode
#     entry tables, function-pointer types) with identical semantics.
InheritParentConfig: true
Checks: >-
  bugprone-*,
  cert-*,
  misc-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  readability-*,
  -misc-no-recursion,
  -performance-enum-size,
  -cert-dcl50-cpp,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -modernize-use-auto,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -modernize-use-using
